            <ArticleTitle>The use of the &quot;Bi-Digital O-Ring Test&quot; to determine whether or not to give acupuncture in pain conditions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The &quot;Bi-Digital O-Ring Test&quot; was used as a guide in determining the modality of treatment of pain conditions. Seven cases are presented in which patients came primarily for acupuncture. They were not treated with acupuncture; instead, they were given antibiotic therapy because the Bi-Digital O-Ring Test had revealed the presence of infection. The antibiotic therapy resulted in dramatic improvement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
